```dart
/// Fastest wrap time over [runs] executions (one untimed warm-up first).
///
/// The growth assertions sample with the MIN, not the median: scheduler
/// steals can only ADD wall time, so the fastest observed run is the
/// least-contended estimate of the true cost at each size — the same
/// principle that gates across attempts, applied within them (gh-1532
/// follow-up: on a heavily loaded arm64 shard a steal window can span
/// ≥3 of 5 runs in EVERY attempt, inflating every attempt median; the
/// per-size min still finds the clean run).
double minWrapMs(String line, int width, {int runs = 5, ElapsedUs? elapsedUs}) {
  final measure = elapsedUs ?? _stopwatchUs;
  wrapAnsiLine(line, width); // JIT warm-up, untimed
  var min = double.infinity;
  for (var i = 0; i < runs; i++) {
    final t = measure(() => wrapAnsiLine(line, width)) / 1000.0;
    if (t < min) min = t;
  }
  return min;
}
```

And in expectLinearGrowth use minWrapMs. Update dartdocs of expectLinearGrowth + the _growthAttempts doc.

